    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Saint‑Martin Collegiate Church, founded in the 14th century, reflects the bishop’s limited power after capitulations and peace treaties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.liege.be/en/discover/tourism/discover-liege/history-of-liege/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bartholomew’s Collegiate Church was established between 1010 and 1015 outside Liège’s original city walls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitezliege.be/en"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Liège waffles are denser and sweeter than Brussels waffles, thanks to a brioche‑based dough and pearl sugar that caramelizes when grilled.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li%C3%A8ge_waffle"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The deeper divots and rounded shape of a Liège waffle give it a chewier bite, while Brussels waffles stay lighter and crispier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li%C3%A8ge_waffle"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The 19th‑century Montagne de Bueren climbs 374 steps, linking Liège’s citadel with the city centre in a remarkable engineering feat.",
